DTSTART:20250524T010000Z
DTEND:20250524T023000Z
DTSTAMP:20250524T010000Z
UID:pHZhDTtGg4
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 80 mins (1h20m)\n\nIn this amazing slice of film her
 story\, learn the legacy of women directors who have fought to be seen and
  heard and have their films preserved…and how to not let the next genera
 tion get lost in the same inequitable and homogenized system. Producer He
 idi Lasi scheduled to attend. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festi
 val/know-her-name\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • SIFF Cinema Uptown House 3 (S
 un 25 May\, 5:00 PM)\n\nFilm is also being streamed.
LOCATION:Shoreline CC Theater\, 16101 Greenwood Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:I Am Nevenka
DTSTART:20250524T033000Z
DTEND:20250524T053500Z
DTSTAMP:20250524T033000Z
UID:0GsFQrnO48
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 112 mins (1h52m)\n\nNevenka Fernández\, the town’
 s finance councilor\, is relentlessly pursued by the mayor\, a man used to
  always getting what he wants politically and personally. Nevenka decides 
 to report him\, turning her courageous fight into Spain’s first #MeToo c
 ase. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/i-am-nevenka\n\nAlso p
 laying at:\n  • SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1 (Wed 21 May\, 1:00 PM)
LOCATION:Shoreline CC Theater\, 16101 Greenwood Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Salsa Lives
DTSTART:20250524T193000Z
DTEND:20250524T212500Z
DTSTAMP:20250524T193000Z
UID:O07qBcjOhR
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 101 mins (1h41m)\n\nThe rhythms\, passion\, and ener
 gy of Salsa do not recognize borders. Born in the vibrant streets of New Y
 ork\, it conquered and reigned in Cali. Featuring Salsa legends like Rub
 én Blades and Henry Fiol\, this illuminating journey shows how entire ge
 nerations have celebrated their common identity through music and dance. L
 overs of Latin music of a variety of genres will want to attend the May 23
  screening for a chance to win a pair of tickets to the Edmonds Center for
  the Arts' "Selena Experience." And if you live for salsa\, shimmy on down
  to the May 24 screening for some live salsa dancing and instruction by Cl
 ub Sur. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/salsa-lives\n\nAlso
  playing at:\n  • SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2 (Fri 23 May\, 5:45 PM)\n\nF
 ilm is also being streamed.
LOCATION:Shoreline CC Theater\, 16101 Greenwood Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Flamingos: Life After the Meteorite
DTSTART:20250524T223000Z
DTEND:20250525T000500Z
DTSTAMP:20250524T223000Z
UID:ZPlsCmmMHQ
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 83 mins (1h23m)\n\nFinding the right partner\, the r
 ight place\, and the ideal time to create a family is the most decisive ta
 sk in nature. Instinct\, love\, and risk are intertwined in this unforgett
 able journey of the Caribbean flamingo in its most delicate period of exis
 tence\; a journey at once surprising\, enthralling\, and deeply inspiring.
  Director Lorenzo Hagerman and producer Jose Cohen scheduled to attend. A 
 few lucky animal lovers will win zoo passes at the May 23 screening\, cour
 tesy of Woodland Park Zoo. Then\, before the May 24 screening\, stop by th
 e Birds Connect Seattle table to learn about their conservation work\, pic
 k up advocacy materials\, and get a rare close-up look at real bird skin s
 pecimens. Expert volunteers will be waiting to chat all things birds with 
 you! Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/flamingos-life-after-t
 he-meteorite\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • AMC Pacific Place 11 (Fri 23 May\,
  6:30 PM)\n\nFilm is also being streamed.
LOCATION:Shoreline CC Theater\, 16101 Greenwood Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Botanist
DTSTART:20250525T010000Z
DTEND:20250525T025000Z
DTSTAMP:20250525T010000Z
UID:3w9LgByumW
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 96 mins (1h36m)\n\nIn Jing Yi’s fantastical\, lush
 ly framed drama set in rural northwestern China\, a lonely 13-year-old Kaz
 akh boy in touch with the wonders of nature befriends a local Han girl\, o
 nly for the call of the modern outside world to come calling. Sponsored by
 :\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/the-botanist\n\nAlso playing at:\n  •
  SIFF Cinema Downtown (Fri 23 May\, 3:30 PM)
LOCATION:Shoreline CC Theater\, 16101 Greenwood Avenue North
END:VEVENT
