DTSTART:20250525T033000Z
DTEND:20250525T053000Z
DTSTAMP:20250525T033000Z
UID:CsMRduu5x1
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 106 mins (1h46m)\n\nChatila and Reda are Palestinian
  refugees stuck in Athens\, trying to figure out how to get to Germany\, h
 ow to stay alive in the meanwhile\, and how to do it all without losing th
 eir humanity.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/to-a-land-unknown\n\nAlso p
 laying at:\n  • AMC Pacific Place 11 (Fri 23 May\, 1:15 PM)
LOCATION:Shoreline CC Theater\, 16101 Greenwood Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Familiar Touch
DTSTART:20250525T200000Z
DTEND:20250525T214500Z
DTSTAMP:20250525T200000Z
UID:SrHdMDV3jo
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 91 mins (1h31m)\n\nRuth Goldman (Broadway legend Kat
 hleen Chalfant) has been living with dementia for some time\, and the time
  has come to place her in an assisted living facility. But while this may 
 seem like the end\, for her it represents something like a new beginning i
 n this poignant\, Venice Film Festival-winning drama. Sponsored by:\n\nhtt
 ps://www.siff.net/festival/familiar-touch\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • SIFF 
 Cinema Uptown House 1 (Sun 18 May\, 6:00 PM)
LOCATION:Shoreline CC Theater\, 16101 Greenwood Avenue North
END:VEVENT
